# ── Renders ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything here is regenerable from the source + the conformed media in public/.
# It is also large: a full out/ tree is over 1 GB, and GitHub hard-rejects any single
# file over 100 MB — the ProRes master alone is ~995 MB.
out/

# ── Dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ── Raw camera originals ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately NOT committed. Two reasons:
#   1. Size — 146 MB across three files, and IMG_9305.MOV alone is 95.6 MB, right at
#      GitHub's 100 MB hard limit.
#   2. Consent — this is unedited footage of an identifiable person in their own home.
#      Anyone with access to the repo can see it, forever, including in git history.
# The CONFORMED, graded clips in public/footage/ ARE committed, so a teammate can open
# Remotion Studio, edit and re-render immediately without these files. They are only
# needed to re-run conform.sh from scratch (different in-point or grade).
# See docs/SHARING.md for how to hand them over separately if that is ever wanted.
incoming/

# ── Local pipeline bookkeeping ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
scripts/.state/
*.log

# ── OS / editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# ── Verification stills ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frame dumps used while checking layout and cursor alignment. Useful locally, not
# part of the deliverable.
out/check/
